  "id": "Compound::DB00961 - Gene::6336",
  "verbalization": "Mepivacaine, a local anesthetic, is shown to bind to multiple voltage-gated sodium channels, specifically Scn8a, Scn4a, and Scn3a, which are all involved in sodium channel activity. This binding is consistent across three distinct paths, each with a high final score, suggesting a strong and reliable interaction. The shared involvement of these channels in sodium channel activity and their subsequent participation in the activity of Scn10a indicates a mechanistic link between Mepivacaine and Scn10a. The evidence suggests that Mepivacaine may modulate the function of Scn10a through its interaction with these sodium channels, potentially affecting neuronal excitability. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Mepivacaine exerts its effects on Scn10a via a mechanism involving sodium channel activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
